  "description": "In-memory actor runtime for Elarion: plain classes marked [Actor] become keyed, mailbox-protected state machines with source-generated typed facades (Orleans-style single-threaded execution, opt-in [Reentrant] interleaving, idle passivation, per-activation DI scopes). Single-node vertical concurrency primitive — clustering is deliberately out of scope (use Orleans/Akka.NET/Proto.Actor when you need a cluster).",
